WEBVTT

00:08.380 --> 00:10.360
This is the entrance to the station.

00:10.360 --> 00:10.990
What?

00:17.260 --> 00:22.000
The new moon sits in the heart of blackness, 
being stained darker and darker.

00:22.000 --> 00:27.000
The arrow of the crescent moon shoots 
to the east, racing faster and faster.

00:27.410 --> 00:32.300
The half moon sinks, and for a moment, 
it touches, growing rounder and rounder.

00:32.760 --> 00:37.900
Chasing the shadow of the night of the 
full moon, around and around they go.

01:00.790 --> 01:02.290
Ren-nii!

01:08.060 --> 01:09.350
Adashino-kun.

01:09.350 --> 01:11.040
That's Sumireko-san, isn't it?

01:11.460 --> 01:14.480
Thank you for looking after Oto for me.

01:14.480 --> 01:17.060
Don't worry about it. We had fun.

01:17.060 --> 01:18.720
Did you?

01:18.720 --> 01:19.560
But...

01:21.010 --> 01:24.260
How could you go to the bathhouse without me?!

01:24.260 --> 01:29.320
I mean, duh. Any bathhouse event 
is going to be without you.

01:29.320 --> 01:31.610
Say it isn't so!

01:31.610 --> 01:35.570
Wow. Even with half your 
face covered in bandages,

01:35.570 --> 01:38.150
I can tell your expression 
is filled with despair.

01:41.960 --> 01:44.580
Are your eyes all right?

01:44.900 --> 01:46.460
Would you believe it?

01:46.460 --> 01:50.600
It turns out they'll be healed instantly 
if I bathe with a curvy woman!

01:50.600 --> 01:53.090
So you're saying it's an incurable disease.

01:53.380 --> 01:55.190
Is that true, Ren-nii?

01:55.190 --> 01:56.850
Will you feel sorry for me if it is?

01:56.850 --> 02:01.270
More importantly, what do you 
think about the Curiosity?

02:01.270 --> 02:03.590
The one reported by... Shizuku-san, was it?

02:03.590 --> 02:07.610
Without seeing the video she has, 
I can't say anything for certain,

02:08.490 --> 02:10.470
but have you heard this story?

02:15.570 --> 02:20.370
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

02:15.570 --> 02:20.370
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

03:40.990 --> 03:44.370
<b>A Curiosity, a Maid, and a Cultured Young Lady</b>

03:41.840 --> 03:47.250
In June 2014, there was an incident 
in Hualien County in eastern Taiwan.

03:44.990 --> 03:47.250
<b>\hHualien County\h</b>

03:47.660 --> 03:50.830
An eighty-year-old woman 
who was there on a tour

03:50.830 --> 03:53.750
said she was going to the 
bathroom and disappeared.

03:54.690 --> 03:57.820
She was seen on security camera footage,

03:57.820 --> 04:00.310
which showed her going 
somewhere of her own will.

04:00.810 --> 04:05.370
Though the search continued, 
they couldn't figure out where she'd gone.

04:05.370 --> 04:07.520
However, four days after that...

04:08.190 --> 04:12.610
The woman was found in a faraway 
cave and was safely rescued.

04:13.120 --> 04:17.250
It was a place that couldn't be reached 
without crossing a raging river.

04:17.790 --> 04:21.540
There was no way an elderly person 
would have the stamina to get there.

04:21.540 --> 04:23.030
Strange, isn't it?

04:23.560 --> 04:27.040
Even stranger were the details 
of her disappearance.

04:27.750 --> 04:32.240
According to the woman, a girl in 
red clothes had brought her there.

04:37.390 --> 04:39.710
A Curiosity that's a girl in red clothes?

04:40.300 --> 04:42.570
That's right. I've heard of this!

04:42.570 --> 04:44.310
I'm pretty sure it was called...

04:44.340 --> 04:47.060
<b>\hHong Yi Xiao Nu Hai\h
(Little Girl in Red)</b>

04:44.620 --> 04:47.060
"Hong yi xiao nu hai."

04:47.380 --> 04:52.360
The hong yi xiao nu hai is a very 
famous urban legend in Taiwan.

04:53.380 --> 04:58.200
In 1998, a video broadcast 
on an occultism show

04:58.200 --> 05:00.090
led to widespread knowledge of it.

05:00.520 --> 05:06.830
Originally, in Taiwan, there were many names 
for Curiosities that led people away.

05:06.830 --> 05:08.830
That Curiosity...

05:09.500 --> 05:12.460
Does it return the people it takes?

05:12.460 --> 05:15.460
Yes. The woman was unharmed.

05:15.460 --> 05:16.820
I see.

05:17.330 --> 05:21.470
I'm glad. Because there were those 
who kept up the search,

05:21.820 --> 05:24.480
and those who made a place 
for her to come home to,

05:24.480 --> 05:26.740
she was able to return.

05:28.970 --> 05:32.730
I want to help Shizuku-san! 
Please let me join the search!

05:32.730 --> 05:35.730
No. It's too great a burden 
for you to handle.

05:36.550 --> 05:39.510
But why? You have no problem 
working with the apartment wife!

05:39.510 --> 05:43.030
Sumireko-san may be a virgin, 
but she's also a full-fledged adult.

05:43.030 --> 05:44.440
She and you are not the same.

05:44.440 --> 05:45.740
Hey, can it.

05:45.740 --> 05:47.420
You can't do it, Oto.

05:51.870 --> 05:53.000
Fine!

05:53.000 --> 05:55.710
I'll go search for her without you!

05:56.750 --> 05:59.250
What are you saying? Stop, Oto!

05:59.560 --> 06:00.580
Oto!

06:09.910 --> 06:12.310
You've really done it this time, Adashino-kun.

06:12.310 --> 06:14.520
She looked pretty upset.

06:14.520 --> 06:16.010
Sumireko-san....

06:17.140 --> 06:20.950
Wh-Wh-Wh...

06:20.950 --> 06:23.430
Wh-What do I do?!

06:23.430 --> 06:25.540
That sounded like some kind of engine noise.

06:25.540 --> 06:29.540
What do I do? Oto hates me!

06:29.900 --> 06:33.890
That's the kind of move a dad would pull 
only to earn his teenage daughter's ire.

06:33.890 --> 06:37.950
Don't worry. I'm sure she'll understand 
by the time she gets married.

06:37.950 --> 06:39.040
Oto's getting married?

06:39.040 --> 06:41.440
To whom? I'll kill the bastard!

06:41.440 --> 06:43.050
Hey, calm down!

06:43.050 --> 06:44.550
But...

06:44.820 --> 06:47.290
You really are hopeless, you know that?

06:47.290 --> 06:50.180
Look, just leave Oto-chan to me.

06:50.180 --> 06:51.860
Shumireko-san...

06:53.600 --> 06:58.880
Anyway, why would such a recent legend 
have already made its way to Japan?

07:00.050 --> 07:02.340
The hong yi xiao nu hai...

07:02.340 --> 07:06.330
Even occult enthusiasts like me 
have only heard of it recently.

07:06.330 --> 07:08.200
It's <i>because</i> you've only 
heard of it recently.

07:08.750 --> 07:11.200
I asked an authority on the subject,

07:11.560 --> 07:15.140
and apparently, new gods 
come to dwell in new places.

07:16.020 --> 07:18.500
This area is a little bit unusual.

07:19.720 --> 07:22.170
Well, that doesn't give me 
a good feeling about this.

07:22.170 --> 07:24.610
And it makes me wonder.

07:25.400 --> 07:28.340
As far as I know, the story 
of the hong yi xiao nu hai

07:28.340 --> 07:32.350
never included anything 
about knocking or the rain.

07:49.880 --> 07:51.540
Can I sit next to you?

07:52.020 --> 07:53.120
Okay.

08:05.090 --> 08:06.370
Yes.

08:06.370 --> 08:08.630
Yes, sorry for the trouble.

08:08.630 --> 08:10.920
Then we'll come and see you now.

08:19.140 --> 08:21.150
<b>Maid Café</b>

08:27.940 --> 08:30.790
Welcome home, my lady.

08:34.920 --> 08:36.160
Meow!

08:39.550 --> 08:41.860
I didn't think you'd be <i>that</i> surprised.

08:41.860 --> 08:43.420
Sorry 'bout that.

08:44.160 --> 08:47.000
Shizuku-san, is this where you work?

08:47.000 --> 08:49.300
I'm a maid. Cute, right?

08:51.780 --> 08:54.380
We can't really talk here. 
Let's go somewhere else.

09:02.810 --> 09:05.190
Thanks for coming all the way here.

09:05.190 --> 09:06.070
What brings you?

09:06.430 --> 09:09.190
I'm going to find Tomoko-san.

09:09.710 --> 09:12.230
So please tell me more about her.

09:12.230 --> 09:15.200
Where she worked, her movement 
patterns, her circle of friends...

09:15.200 --> 09:17.200
Tell me everything you can!

09:20.970 --> 09:22.960
Meow!

09:29.130 --> 09:30.590
Who do you take me for?

09:31.440 --> 09:32.720
Go on, beat it!

09:33.120 --> 09:34.340
Shizuku-san...

09:40.000 --> 09:42.980
My eyes can see the traces 
left by Curiosities.

09:43.520 --> 09:50.360
If I can use them to track the places where 
Tomoko-san has been, I might find something.

09:50.750 --> 09:54.540
So please, tell me about Tomoko-san!

09:56.490 --> 09:59.490
<b></b>Search

09:59.490 --> 10:02.320
You did it, Oto-chan! 
I'd expect nothing less from you.

10:02.320 --> 10:04.000
Th-Thank you.

10:05.390 --> 10:07.730
Next, I'm going to go through these in order!

10:08.750 --> 10:10.910
Roger that, boss.

10:29.480 --> 10:31.680
No leads, huh?

10:32.420 --> 10:33.740
Any idea what to do next?

10:37.770 --> 10:41.500
I gotta say, though... her circle 
of friends is bigger than I expected.

10:41.850 --> 10:43.740
It's not just her coworkers.

10:43.740 --> 10:47.020
Even the clerk at the convenience store 
she frequented is worried for her.

10:47.540 --> 10:49.950
Maybe she wasn't really 
alone in the world after all.

10:51.000 --> 10:56.010
But the only one who looked 
for Tomoko-san was Shizuku-san.

10:56.760 --> 10:57.960
Take that!

11:00.510 --> 11:01.980
White, as I thought.

11:01.980 --> 11:03.330
Shizuku-san!

11:03.790 --> 11:07.060
Hey, you guys. Let's go eat some ramen.

11:08.270 --> 11:10.520
<b></b>Chinese Cuisine

11:08.270 --> 11:10.520
<b></b>Tatsuta

11:11.380 --> 11:12.610
It's so good!

11:12.610 --> 11:13.530
Right?

11:16.860 --> 11:19.030
So, come up with anything yet?

11:20.070 --> 11:21.780
No, nothing.

11:21.780 --> 11:24.540
I see. Well, I kinda expected that.

11:26.160 --> 11:29.920
Um, what kind of friend was Tomoko-san?

11:29.920 --> 11:32.550
Huh? Well...

11:34.450 --> 11:37.800
Both of us had frayed relationships 
with our families,

11:38.170 --> 11:40.130
so we moved here from the countryside.

11:40.130 --> 11:42.060
We were roommates.

11:42.870 --> 11:46.060
We'd split one packet of instant 
ramen between us...

11:46.840 --> 11:49.680
Carry a kotatsu that'd been 
dumped back to our place...

11:50.810 --> 11:53.760
And when anything stupid happened,

11:53.760 --> 11:57.070
the first person I'd want 
to tell about it was her.

11:57.610 --> 12:00.160
When Tomoko started attending 
cosmetology school,

12:00.160 --> 12:02.080
we moved out to different places.

12:02.080 --> 12:04.800
The truth is, I wasn't in contact 
with her very much.

12:05.830 --> 12:09.580
On that day a year ago, I got a message 
from her for the first time in ages.

12:10.360 --> 12:13.330
She was grinning triumphantly, 
saying she finally got a job in a salon.

12:14.210 --> 12:16.420
I don't know if it's a Curiosity or what,

12:16.420 --> 12:18.090
but I want it to give Tomoko back.

12:19.030 --> 12:23.040
Ever since that day, 
time has stopped moving for me.

12:27.220 --> 12:28.920
I'm gonna get going.

12:28.920 --> 12:32.230
A runt like you's gotta eat more, 
or you'll never grow up big and strong.

12:32.230 --> 12:34.300
Wait, Shizuku-chan.

12:35.900 --> 12:38.100
There's something I want you to tell me.

12:38.100 --> 12:41.570
What day and month was that video taken?

12:41.990 --> 12:45.740
<b>Laws Regarding Unsolved Cases</b>

12:49.400 --> 12:52.810
If you'd like to access the database, 
booth two is available.

12:53.500 --> 12:56.510
<b>Missing
Persons List</b>

12:59.850 --> 13:02.060
Hang on. Is this what I think it is?

13:09.430 --> 13:11.740
Bye, Occhan!

13:11.740 --> 13:13.310
See you tomorrow!

13:13.310 --> 13:15.570
Good day to you, Nodoka!

13:27.080 --> 13:29.580
<b>Maid Café</b>

13:33.580 --> 13:37.590
<b>Getting Ready to Serve You</b>

13:36.120 --> 13:37.590
Head Maid, we have a problem!

13:37.910 --> 13:41.990
Nagano-san's asking for the day off 
because her child has a fever!

13:41.990 --> 13:44.850
And we're already shorthanded today!

13:45.490 --> 13:50.840
But supporting each other through our 
family issues is an ironclad rule here!

13:55.260 --> 13:57.560
You again, Adashino Oto?

13:57.910 --> 14:00.410
I don't have time for you 
right now. Just go home.

14:00.410 --> 14:02.630
Wait, please, Head Maid!

14:05.310 --> 14:07.940
She's exactly what we need, don't you think?

14:07.940 --> 14:10.250
It'll look wonderful on her! 
There's no question!

14:10.250 --> 14:13.880
I can't be a maid! I couldn't possibly!

14:14.570 --> 14:16.500
Now, now. I'm counting on you.

14:16.970 --> 14:20.260
As thanks, I'll treat you 
to a deluxe parfait.

14:20.260 --> 14:22.260
A deluxe parfait?

14:22.260 --> 14:26.260
<b>KISARAGI</b>

14:31.270 --> 14:32.390
<b>Sumire</b>

14:31.270 --> 14:32.390
<b>Sumireko-san</b>

14:32.390 --> 14:34.270
<b>Sumireko-san</b>

14:32.390 --> 14:34.270
Hello? Sumireko-san?

14:34.270 --> 14:36.200
<i>Do you have a minute to talk?</i>

14:36.200 --> 14:39.520
I do, though I must apologize 
for my half-dressed state.

14:39.520 --> 14:41.840
<i>Fortunately, I can't see you.</i>

14:41.840 --> 14:46.030
Thank you for going with Oto yesterday.

14:46.030 --> 14:48.530
<b>Sumireko-san</b>

14:46.030 --> 14:48.530
<i>Is Oto-chan nearby?</i>

14:48.530 --> 14:52.260
<i>She might have given up. 
She went to school without a fuss.</i>

14:52.260 --> 14:56.790
That's good. Listen to what 
I'm about to say, Adashino-kun.

14:57.600 --> 15:00.960
At the city library, I looked up cases 
that wouldn't appear in national papers—

15:00.960 --> 15:04.990
local cases of disappearances 
and missing persons.

15:05.450 --> 15:11.060
On the same exact day that Tomoko-san 
went missing, a woman's body was found.

15:07.550 --> 15:11.060
<b>Unidentified Body Found</b>

15:11.060 --> 15:13.940
A body? You don't think it was Tomoko-san?

15:13.940 --> 15:15.310
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

15:15.840 --> 15:18.310
The body wasn't Tomoko-san's.

15:18.600 --> 15:22.870
It was discovered in a landslide caused 
by several days of continuous rain.

15:23.710 --> 15:26.820
The time was confirmed by cameras 
installed at the location.

15:26.820 --> 15:32.700
<b>Have You Seen This Person?</b>

15:27.500 --> 15:32.700
The thing is, a search request for that woman 
had been submitted half a year before that.

15:32.950 --> 15:34.700
<i>Interesting, isn't it?</i>

15:35.260 --> 15:39.250
I compiled a list of three years' 
worth of missing persons

15:39.250 --> 15:41.710
and arranged a timeline 
of cases and accidents.

15:42.230 --> 15:45.120
<i>When I did, I realized the connection.</i>

15:45.540 --> 15:46.710
<i>The search requests,</i>

15:46.710 --> 15:51.720
missing person reports, and body 
discoveries overlapped in certain places.

15:52.380 --> 15:55.250
On the days when missing 
persons disappeared,

15:55.250 --> 15:58.700
the bodies of other 
missing persons were found.

15:59.230 --> 16:01.590
I went back and found six cases.

16:01.590 --> 16:03.650
All of them happened on rainy days.

16:03.650 --> 16:07.240
It's possible there are others 
that I didn't notice, too.

16:07.240 --> 16:12.610
You get it, right? Basically, when someone 
disappears, someone else is found.

16:09.610 --> 16:13.370
<b>Discovery</b>

16:09.610 --> 16:13.370
<b>X Month Y Day</b>

16:10.370 --> 16:13.370
<b>Disappearance</b>

16:10.370 --> 16:13.370
<b>Discovery</b>

16:10.370 --> 16:13.370
<b>Y Month Y Day</b>

16:11.120 --> 16:13.370
<b>Disappearance</b>

16:11.120 --> 16:13.370
<b>Discovery</b>

16:11.120 --> 16:13.370
<b>Z Month X Day</b>

16:11.870 --> 16:13.370
<b>Disappearance</b>

16:11.870 --> 16:13.370
<b>Discovery</b>

16:11.870 --> 16:13.370
<b>Y Month Z Day</b>

16:12.620 --> 16:13.370
<b>Disappearance</b>

16:12.620 --> 16:13.370
<b>Tomoko</b>

16:14.370 --> 16:15.870
It's like a baton relay.

16:19.370 --> 16:20.870
I see.

16:25.120 --> 16:26.380
<i>Sumireko-san?</i>

16:27.320 --> 16:28.790
This is the worst-case scenario.

16:28.790 --> 16:32.510
There's only one conclusion 
we can draw from this.

16:35.320 --> 16:38.140
Welcome home, masters.

16:39.470 --> 16:40.650
Are you new?

16:40.650 --> 16:42.830
My name is Otohime.

16:43.230 --> 16:45.090
P-Pweeze have a sheet...

16:45.090 --> 16:45.860
She fumbled her words.

16:45.860 --> 16:46.900
She's adorable.

16:49.230 --> 16:50.410
Moe, moe!

16:50.410 --> 16:51.410
Moe, moe!

16:51.790 --> 16:52.900
Kyun, kyun!

16:52.900 --> 16:54.030
Kyun, kyun!

16:54.030 --> 16:55.290
Shake, shake!

16:55.290 --> 16:56.290
Shake, shake!

16:56.290 --> 16:57.540
Rattle, rattle!

16:57.540 --> 16:58.540
Rattle, rattle!

17:05.510 --> 17:08.170
I'll draw my favorite animal, okay?

17:08.490 --> 17:11.430
Get yummy, get yummy—Huh?

17:17.400 --> 17:18.930
I'm so sorry!

17:18.930 --> 17:22.030
At first glance, she seems like an 
accident-prone mistake of a maid.

17:22.030 --> 17:25.110
But the customers are smiling 
because she's just too cute.

17:25.110 --> 17:26.190
She's perfect.

17:27.480 --> 17:29.190
I have something to report, as well.

17:29.860 --> 17:33.540
I looked into the hong yi xiao nu hai again.

17:34.580 --> 17:37.050
Do you remember what I said 
about the knocking?

17:37.630 --> 17:39.950
I think I've found something regarding that.

17:40.970 --> 17:45.910
At a certain university in Taiwan, there's 
a story about the hong yi xiao nu hai.

17:47.410 --> 17:52.250
When night comes, a young female spirit 
in red clothes invites people to play,

17:52.830 --> 17:55.840
and if you accept her invitation, 
you lose your life.

17:56.660 --> 18:00.510
Among the variations of the story, 
there are cases where she knocks first.

18:01.020 --> 18:02.230
This must be it.

18:02.540 --> 18:04.990
As for why it's associated with rain,

18:04.990 --> 18:08.240
that's likely due to tales of spirits 
long said to abduct people near the water:

18:08.520 --> 18:11.150
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

18:08.520 --> 18:11.150
<b>Shui Gui
(Water Ghost)</b>

18:08.770 --> 18:10.030
the shui gui.

18:10.480 --> 18:13.170
During its journey across 
the ocean to this very town,

18:13.170 --> 18:16.060
the legend became conflated 
with various other imagery.

18:16.060 --> 18:18.730
And so the hong yi xiao nu hai transformed.

18:19.490 --> 18:22.240
<b>K</b>

18:19.490 --> 18:22.240
<b>I</b>

18:19.490 --> 18:22.240
<b>S</b>

18:19.490 --> 18:22.240
<b>A</b>

18:19.490 --> 18:22.240
<b>R</b>

18:19.490 --> 18:22.240
<b>A</b>

18:19.490 --> 18:22.240
<b>G</b>

18:19.490 --> 18:22.240
<b>I</b>

18:19.870 --> 18:22.250
So that tales of it would be scarier,

18:22.250 --> 18:24.590
people built on them and added to them,

18:24.590 --> 18:26.930
and the end result of their 
storytelling was this.

18:28.200 --> 18:32.740
Finally, the shui gui has one more 
characteristic we can't afford to ignore.

18:33.470 --> 18:36.450
The data you found convinced me of it.

18:37.290 --> 18:39.250
Good work today, Oto-chan.

18:40.240 --> 18:42.380
Thank you for your hard work, Senpai!

18:42.380 --> 18:45.550
You really helped us out! 
You're the best, Oto-chan!

18:45.550 --> 18:49.520
Your magic surpassed mine on your first day. 
You've utterly defeated me.

18:49.520 --> 18:52.240
But all I did was make mistakes.

18:52.740 --> 18:54.530
Thank you!

18:54.530 --> 18:55.870
You're such a good girl.

18:55.870 --> 18:58.860
We asked the impossible of you, 
but you're thanking us.

18:58.860 --> 19:00.520
Could she be an angel in the flesh?

19:01.150 --> 19:02.540
Please don't!

19:02.960 --> 19:04.770
It's only natural that we'd be grateful.

19:04.770 --> 19:07.790
If we weren't, the head maid 
would knock us into next week.

19:08.770 --> 19:12.550
The head maid? What kind 
of person is Shizuku-san?

19:13.290 --> 19:14.300
The head maid?

19:14.300 --> 19:17.460
She's dependable, she's kind, 
and she's understanding.

19:17.460 --> 19:20.630
But she gives off an aura saying 
not to get too close, right?

19:20.630 --> 19:21.420
She totally does.

19:21.420 --> 19:24.310
She's wary of others, and she's actually 
uncomfortable around strangers.

19:24.310 --> 19:27.080
To sum it up, I guess 
she's sort of like a cat.

19:27.080 --> 19:29.330
And she'd be the boss of the strays, right?

19:30.410 --> 19:34.320
If you're gonna badmouth me, 
do it somewhere I can't hear you.

19:35.820 --> 19:38.100
Good work today, Adashino Oto.

19:38.100 --> 19:40.070
Here's the promised deluxe parfait.

19:40.490 --> 19:43.080
Once you've changed, come eat it in my room.

19:43.080 --> 19:44.950
<b>Shizuku's Room</b>

19:44.290 --> 19:48.120
In other words, I believe we have 
arrived at the same conclusion.

19:48.120 --> 19:49.960
<i>If we're right, then Oto-chan is...</i>

19:50.700 --> 19:53.460
<i>Can I ask you to take care 
of her, Sumireko-san?</i>

19:53.460 --> 19:55.920
Thank you for waiting, my lady.

19:55.920 --> 19:58.220
This is our deluxe parfait.

19:58.220 --> 19:59.690
Thank you!

19:59.690 --> 20:01.470
Eat as much as you like!

20:01.470 --> 20:02.480
Another!

20:03.010 --> 20:03.720
That was fast!

20:03.720 --> 20:05.730
Thank you for the feast.

20:05.730 --> 20:09.480
Man, you're one heck of an eater. 
It's somehow refreshing.

20:17.040 --> 20:18.560
Hey, Adashino Oto...

20:20.160 --> 20:21.980
I gotta apologize for being mean to you.

20:22.440 --> 20:23.490
I'm sorry.

20:26.400 --> 20:30.380
While I searched for Tomoko on my own, 
people said all kinds of things to me.

20:30.750 --> 20:32.830
Some people just pretended 
they were worried.

20:33.360 --> 20:36.580
Some people even said I must have done it.

20:37.690 --> 20:41.140
I thought you were someone who'd just 
go through the motions, like them.

20:43.000 --> 20:46.140
I was really happy to meet you, Shizuku-san.

20:46.960 --> 20:48.820
My brother and I got lost,

20:48.820 --> 20:52.110
and before we knew it, we were 
somewhere completely unfamiliar.

20:52.110 --> 20:55.280
We waited for help, but no one came.

20:55.280 --> 20:57.650
That's why my brother is 
pushing himself so hard.

20:58.170 --> 21:00.650
"Why isn't anyone looking for us?" I wondered.

21:01.210 --> 21:04.300
"Does that mean no one needs us?"

21:05.120 --> 21:07.160
So I was really happy to see

21:07.160 --> 21:11.290
that there are people like you who search 
so hard for those who go missing.

21:11.290 --> 21:12.920
Adashino Oto...

21:14.520 --> 21:18.050
I'm sure you'll see Tomoko-san again! 
I want you to see her again!

21:21.420 --> 21:22.800
<b></b>Apartment Wife

21:24.360 --> 21:25.810
What is it, apartment wife?

21:26.160 --> 21:28.930
Oto-chan, are you all right? 
Where are you right now?

21:28.930 --> 21:31.440
Shizuku-san's maid café.

21:33.920 --> 21:35.440
Is something wrong?

21:36.690 --> 21:39.410
Don't go anywhere until I get there, Oto-chan!

21:42.710 --> 21:46.890
What's going on? 
This door leads to the roof.

21:46.890 --> 21:48.960
<i>Don't open the door, no matter who knocks!</i>

21:54.320 --> 21:56.460
<i>The hong yi xiao nu hai...</i>

21:56.460 --> 21:58.160
<i>is Tomoko-san herself!</i>

23:34.980 --> 23:39.980
<b>A Station, Scissors, and a Haircut</b>

23:36.100 --> 23:39.620
Next time: "A Station, 
Scissors, and a Haircut."
